														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1984452">
									

<p>I like this one, but I have two quips.</p>
<p>Firstly, there shouldn't be anything redacted, expunged or otherwise removed from the containment procedure&#8230; if that part of the procedure is unknown, it can't be performed.</p>
<p>Secondly, the containment procedures seem overly detailed. I think we can assume that standard bio-material access restrictions/protocols apply, including quarantine procedures, except perhaps for the addition of O5 approval. HAZMAT containment is fairly well understood, especially by The Foundation, so enumerating everything probably isn't necessary.</p>
<p>I really like the idea that it isn't infectious itself, but that it causes infections. Clever.</p>

							</div>

								
					
